{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games","id":358916,"title":"Looking for ideas on introductory stories for a few different cWoD games.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-04T01:39:57-08:00","id":358916,"title":"Looking for ideas on introductory stories for a few different cWoD games.","content":"Over the next few weeks, I plan on running several introductory stories, 1 each, for a few different cWoD games. As of now, I\u2019m planning on Hunter (the Reckoning), Werewolf, Vampire and Changeling.<br /> <br /> Right now, our gaming group consists of only 2 players familiar with the classic world of darkness (in a general sense) and 2 players that have had some exposure to the system, but not really to any of the games. Out of those 2 players, 1 is familiar with D&amp;D and the other has only role played once, in a game I ran last year, that used the system at its core, but wasn\u2019t any specific game. (I like the WoD system for its ability to make well rounded out human characters)<br /> <br /> So the plan right now, is to have each introduction last only a session or 2, to introduce the themes and concepts of each line and then afterwards we can see which the group enjoyed most and hopefully play that one regularly. I\u2019ve pre-generated 17 characters, all high school students. I\u2019m hoping to go through the transformation (embrace, chrysalis, first change, imbuing, etc.) so the players aren\u2019t top loaded with abilities and can figure things out through game play. Each story will be independent of one another, but using a shared background (the school). So each new story may have new characters, but as we play, the backgrounds will be filled in. Relationships, such as who knows who from before these events will stay and we will build up the school as a setting little by little. All of the characters are tropes (metalhead, cheerleader, etc) just to make it easier on the players. That has already been discussed with each of them and they are all on board.<br /> <br /> So yea\u2026I have a full Hunter story set up, and possible frameworks for Werewolf and Changeling stories. All I can come up with for this sort of thing for Vampire would be centered around a Sabbat siege, as mass embracies, for either side. This is the weakest of the ideas which is why I\u2019m asking for help from the forums. Mind you, if you have ideas for 1 shots for the other game lines listed (Changeling or Werewolf mostly) I\u2019d love to hear them. Or even if someone has an idea on how to run an intro to another game line that won\u2019t over-confuse my players (Demon, Mummy, etc). I am trying to stay away from Wraith with them though, since even talking about the setting had the new players thinking that it might be too depressing or complicated (with Shadowguides) for them.<br /> <br /> Any ideas or feedback would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T02:57:04-08:00","id":358960,"title":"","content":"For Vampire since your doing a high school setting is to do one of those now a days popular but simple plots about a Vampire falling for one of the players and Embracing him/her after which that player could Embrace the rest or something, this is a one shot after all. Sabbat mass Embrace could also work as could them being chosen for one of the Game's for a Sabbat pack or even a game between two packs, the surviving members could be granted the Embrace as a reward. My Priest Ghouled such a survivor once after she had not only proven resourceful but also managed to outwit and beat one of the participating Cainites.<br /> <br /> For Demon, either DtF or DD, you could mesh it up with the Mage part if you managed to imply there were forbidden texts floating about in the school, just have some bunch messing around with such spells and managing to summon a Demon that promptly Possesses one of the summoners which acts as the starting point for the Demon, again the other PC's could then play the would be summoners, now Thralls, or the first one could make them summon up a few of his friends who then possess the rest of the circle or they could even somehow manage to evoke a sort of mass summoning as they unbeknownst to them open up a limited time only open portal to the Abyss through which the future PC's escape to possess either the summoners or just random people about the school.<br /> <br /> The Demon part works best if the Mage part has some sort of Infernalist, or just a dabbler in the infernal as a bad guy who's grimoire the players miss, or just misplace, after getting rid of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 01-04-2015, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:04:27-08:00","id":359091,"title":"","content":"This school sounds like a drama infused masquerade breaking blood bath waiting to happen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T13:33:13-08:00","id":359494,"title":"","content":"I'd consider starting with mortals for the first game - it gives a baseline introduction to the world and the system, and also being a one-shot lets you kill them off, so it also emphasises how different the supernatural characters' POV can be. The characters could also start normal and become Hunters during the adventure.<br /> <br /> Starting with newly Embraced vampires is a good in-character introduction to <b>Vampire</b> as the players learn along with their characters, but they can miss out on the fun of being immortal and powerful. I'd consider a mixed game there, with the more experienced players as vampires with a few years under their belt and the new players as neonates or as mortals that the vampires have to work with. (To balance that out, maybe in the <b>Hunter</b> game the new players' characters are Imbued and the experienced players play mortals?)<br /> <br /> The <b>Werewolf</b> game could connect the others together, as something supernatural from that setting dwells under the school, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T13:35:30-08:00","id":359498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=359091#post359091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This school sounds like a drama infused masquerade breaking blood bath waiting to happen</div> </div> </div> </div>That would still expose the players to the Traditions. Maybe I\u2019ll have the entire group embraced by a neonate that thinks doing so will establish his own domain. Then the session plays out with them running away from the local sheriff after their sire is destroyed.<br /> Maybe even have the PCs all be ghouls, and if they somehow manage to outsmart or take down the sheriff, they could be gifted with the embrace.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T13:47:16-08:00","id":359504,"title":"","content":"Do Hunter the Reckoning very last. Then the players can use newbie Hunters to clean out the school of all the other supernaturals that have cropped up. And either 1) Die at the hands of the characters from the gameline the characters have selected to play or 2) Kill 'em all and survive the High School from Hell if they start having a ton of fun massacring their other characters and decide to go with Hunter.<br /> <br /> Maybe a few survivors from some of the lines... For future nemeses purposes....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T13:50:13-08:00","id":359505,"title":"","content":"Vampire is cool if you have a &quot;climax&quot; of players (in my case happened to a climax with a girl in one sitting), thinking in a game with heterosexual people.<br /> Otherwise it can happen one Lestat and Louis ...<br /> Serious guy never played vampire in a group without females! It is the icing on the cake!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3958,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3958-silverb","user":"Silverb","date":".  edit: correction write 01-04-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3958-silverb","name":"Silverb","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3958_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T16:48:00-08:00","id":359679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=359504#post359504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Hunter the Reckoning very last. Then the players can use newbie Hunters to clean out the school of all the other supernaturals that have cropped up. And either 1) Die at the hands of the characters from the gameline the characters have selected to play or 2) Kill 'em all and survive the High School from Hell if they start having a ton of fun massacring their other characters and decide to go with Hunter.<br /> <br /> Maybe a few survivors from some of the lines... For future nemeses purposes....</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering this, but I think Hunter might be the easiest for players to get and so I'm torn on whether or not to start with Hunter. I was thinking maybe ending with Werewolf (after Vampire) and having the newly changed Garou hunt down the vampires in the school/town. Or if I go with the sheriff idea, having the players hunt down the sheriff after he's killed off their other characters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: btw, thank you guys for the ideas and input so far, it helps a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-04-2015, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T19:59:39-08:00","id":360873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=358960#post358960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For Demon, either DtF or DD, you could mesh it up with the Mage part if you managed to imply there were forbidden texts floating about in the school, just have some bunch messing around with such spells and managing to summon a Demon that promptly Possesses one of the summoners which acts as the starting point for the Demon, again the other PC's could then play the would be summoners, now Thralls, or the first one could make them summon up a few of his friends who then possess the rest of the circle or they could even somehow manage to evoke a sort of mass summoning as they unbeknownst to them open up a limited time only open portal to the Abyss through which the future PC's escape to possess either the summoners or just random people about the school.<br /> <br /> The Demon part works best if the Mage part has some sort of Infernalist, or just a dabbler in the infernal as a bad guy who's grimoire the players miss, or just misplace, after getting rid of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Demon games, my understanding is that you are playing the Demon in question as opposed to any sort of mortal. If this is correct, then that leads into the problem of distancing the intro concept from starting as base mortals. I think it will be a lot easier (on newer players especially) to relate to a mortal character that is undergoing some sort of transformation, rather than having them play a being that existed around the creation on the universe. Though the idea of them playing Thralls could work. What sort of things would a newly summoned demon be having thralls do? (I have the Demon books, but have never actually played, and have only looked through for NPCs for other games)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=359494#post359494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Starting with newly Embraced vampires is a good in-character introduction to <b>Vampire</b> as the players learn along with their characters, but they can miss out on the fun of being immortal and powerful. I'd consider a mixed game there, with the more experienced players as vampires with a few years under their belt and the new players as neonates or as mortals that the vampires have to work with. (To balance that out, maybe in the <b>Hunter</b> game the new players' characters are Imbued and the experienced players play mortals?)</div> </div> </div> </div>From experience, I\u2019ve seen games with deliberate power gaps between players go badly, as someone always feels slighted or underpowered. And even my experienced players don\u2019t have that much experience. One of my players has spent time reading a lot of the books, but hasn\u2019t had the chance to really delve into the game side of most of the game lines. And my other experienced player has played lots of Changeling, but not really any of the other game lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=359494#post359494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The <b>Werewolf</b> game could connect the others together, as something supernatural from that setting dwells under the school, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think for the Werewolf game, I\u2019m going to have the town be a Kinfolk town and have them be on a bus going on a school trip and have the bus ran off the road. Perhaps for the because of the Vampire game. Some of the Werewolf character\u2019s classmates get dragged off to be embraced, and for their first task, the new Garou get sent out to hunt down the new vampire infestation. That way they actually have to track and investigate, and eventually make the decision of whether or not to go through with \u201ccleansing\u201d their newly turned friends and classmates.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silverb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=359505#post359505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire is cool if you have a &quot;climax&quot; of players (in my case happened to a climax with a girl in one sitting), thinking in a game with heterosexual people.<br /> Otherwise it can happen one Lestat and Louis ...<br /> Serious guy never played vampire in a group without females! It is the icing on the cake!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure what you mean by this, can you please explain?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T22:05:16-08:00","id":360981,"title":"","content":"Well quite sadly unless your using DD rules for Demons, and even there a newly summoned Demon can have slight identity issues, Demons without the Legacy Background in DtF identify more with the possessed mortals than they do with their identity as demons, that is without any dot's in the background they are almost as likely to think of themselves as mortals with powers rather than anything of divine origins. Thus by controlling their Legacy amounts you can decide which part of the composite being is in charge, yes it's technically the Demon the whole time but if it has no legacy it is overwhelmed by mortal memories and thinks these as his own. Demon Player's Guide has the details on levels of Legacy and the intermingling of personalities, in short no Legacy or very low Legacy mortal memories dominate ergo mortal personality dominates high legacy mortal memories start to feel like dreams and Demonic/Angelic you starts to be in charge.<br /> <br /> As for Thralls it again depends upon their Demonic masters Legacy, low legacy master will likely ask of more normal things if it ask much of anything at all high legacy master can command them to searching more names to summon others, to seek other people willing to become Thralls or otherwise suitable people for followers etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T22:48:03-08:00","id":361014,"title":"","content":"awesome info, thank you. I'll look into that stuff when I get home and have access to my books. So other than getting to play with the Demon powers, what would you suggest for the theme or story for a short Demon game? Would something like the Reaper TV show work? Where the PCs have to hunt down and re-banish (and how does that work?) an escaped Demon that does have the Legacy background, and thus remembers its nature. I'm just trying to keep these introductions within the general themes presented by the different lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T00:58:21-08:00","id":361072,"title":"","content":"Well I'd probably go with getting to play with Demon powers with perhaps a few hints of remembrance here and there as to establish that there is a lot more to the game than those powers, and in fact there's a lot more about your specific characters, and try to go with a simple plot agaisnt some weaker Earthbounds minions/cult perhaps.<br /> <br /> Actual Banishments etc are the domain of humans mostly Demons can banish each other but that usually involves the death of the current host.<br /> <br /> Just throwing ideas since I'm legendarily bad at running one shots and short games, my convention game continued I think three or four sessions after the convention ended. So just trying to give inspiration and leaving actual execution and how to get things into only one or two sessions to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T03:12:09-08:00","id":361111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=361072#post361072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well I'd probably go with getting to play with Demon powers with perhaps a few hints of remembrance here and there as to establish that there is a lot more to the game than those powers, and in fact there's a lot more about your specific characters, and try to go with a simple plot agaisnt some weaker Earthbounds minions/cult perhaps.<br /> <br /> Actual Banishments etc are the domain of humans mostly Demons can banish each other but that usually involves the death of the current host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, good to know. I didn\u2019t know whether or not Demons could do that sort of thing without killing the host. Curious related question. When a Demon takes over, what happens to the person who was? Do they die (and thus the soul departs)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=361072#post361072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just throwing ideas since I'm legendarily bad at running one shots and short games, my convention game continued I think three or four sessions after the convention ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly relate to this. The first game I played with this group (the one using the WoD system) was supposed to be a short chronicle for fun and to show people the system. I had planned it out for about 4-6 sessions. It lasted a bit over a year of mostly weekly sessions. This is why I\u2019m trying to plan this out as much as possible beforehand. So these stories don\u2019t run too long and we can actually get to play a little of each game.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=361072#post361072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So just trying to give inspiration and leaving actual execution and how to get things into only one or two sessions to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I\u2019m thankful for the help. I\u2019m not normally one to ask for help, but I was/am having trouble coming up with stories for some of the game lines that are short enough to be told in just a handful of scenes. And even if I don\u2019t use ideas presented wholesale, they\u2019ve given me a lot to think about and have served as inspiration.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T04:04:58-08:00","id":361120,"title":"","content":"In DtF the demonic possession happens to individuals that are either dying or have some debilitation of the spirit and soul which means that &quot;normal&quot; people are usually safe from possession, though as normal the Golden Rule applies but even then there should be some chink in the mortals armour some weakness of soul even if only temporarily, like a depression and hopelessness resulting from a series of misfortunes, you were dumped, you house burned down and your close relative all dies within the month etc. In normal circumstances you could recover from that but in this case it might be enough to make you vulnerable to possession.<br /> <br /> As for the normal possession of dying or spiritually debilitated individuals the players guide offers multiple possible answers to what happens to the human soul. When possessing the dying at the moment of death it usually results in the human soul being kicked out with only the lingering memories remaining (this is the default option), but for possessing the still living these are the option given by the demon players guide(DPG) 1) The Living Ghost meaning that the soul remains in the same body as a whispering voice, which can result in all sorts of trouble including it trying to give out false information and even it's activity is open to ST it could only be able to whisper when the demon is tired or sleeping or just high on Faith. 2) Enslave the Soul, in which case hte demon bullies hte human soul into submission and can therefore force it to give away information or even Faith at the ST discretion.<br /> <br /> The latter option opens the door for the question could a powerful human soul do the opposite if so the DPG offers the option of Enslave the Demon in which case the human soul takes over the shared body (for an example the DPG suggest one to look at Hunter: Fall From Grace and the character of John Coaler specifically). It still leaves open the question of whether the two halves in these cases could ever come to equal terms and form a symbiosis of sort.<br /> <br /> Finally it discusses the option of Drive Out the Soul as something of a goal for the Demon to be achieved through ritual, prayer or just rigorous debauched living and again it leaves the consequences of it to the ST. It might mean the 100% return of the Fallens memory which might result in a huge raise in Torment as well since it is the human memories that act as a sort of buffer for the character Torment.<br /> <br /> But yes the default assumption in DtF is that the Demon possesses it's host at the time of it's death and the human soul departs on it's normal course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:12:13-08:00","id":362514,"title":"","content":"Yesterday, 03:59 AM Idpersona<br /> Originally posted by <b>Silverb</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/358916-looking-for-ideas-on-introductory-stories-for-a-few-different-cwod-games?p=359505#post359505\">View Post</a> Vampire is cool if you have a &quot;climax&quot; of players (in my case happened to a climax with a girl in one sitting), thinking in a game with heterosexual people.<br /> Otherwise it can happen one Lestat and Louis ...<br /> Serious guy never played vampire in a group without females! It is the icing on the cake!<br /> I\u2019m not sure what you mean by this, can you please explain?<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\"><b><span style=\"color:#2379b5\">idpersona</span></b></a><br /> <br /> <br /> I could not get the quote!<br /> <br /> I meant that an interest among the players can be a spice, the interest of character converge with the players, occurring a &quot;true love&quot;.<br /> Many players enjoy playing vampire like a Highlander, I think that style of play does not work with the female audience, you said you would have a girl in your group ... well maybe some girls like to hunt vampires, when I played vampire, in my party the girls were the vampires and we poor men were not hunters were ok ... did not happen love, but it was hot. In fact no one picked anyone but flourished fantasies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3958-silverb","name":"Silverb","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3958_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}